  "descriptionRussian": "Образование и употребление",
  "imageName": "arrow.left.arrow.right.square",
  "intro": "Present passive participles describe something BEING DONE (now/generally). They replace 'который + passive': книга, которую читают → читаемая книга (a book being read). Formation: 1st person plural present stem + -ЕМЫЙ (1st conj) or -ИМЫЙ (2nd conj). Читаем → читаемый. Любим → любимый. These are less common than other participles and often become adjectives: любимый (favorite), уважаемый (respected).",
  "rules": [
    "Present passive participles are the rarest type — many verbs cannot form them, and they sound very formal/bookish.",
    "Several have become everyday adjectives: любимый (favorite), уважаемый (dear/respected), невидимый (invisible).",
    "Only transitive imperfective verbs can form present passive participles — intransitive and perfective verbs cannot.",
    "In modern Russian, these are mostly used in formal writing, academic texts, and set phrases like 'Уважаемые коллеги!'"
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Изучаемый нами предмет очень интересный. (The subject being studied by us is very interesting.)",
    "Это мой любимый фильм. (This is my favorite film.), adjective use",
    "Уважаемые коллеги! (Dear colleagues!), formal address",
    "Видимый результат налицо. (The visible result is evident.)"
  ],
